# The whole play, before anyone has been honest about it. Every named thing here is
# something somebody once wanted, which is why the bulk is not a strawman: the work
# really does arrive this full.

bulk cast.hero
bulk cast.brother
bulk act1.opening
bulk act1.dinner
bulk act2.ballroom
bulk act3.letter

# She reads it twice and it is the only time she does. This is not a preference, it is
# the reason the play is about her, so nothing downstream is allowed to take it.
keep act3.letter because she reads it twice and it is the only time she does

carve act1.opening because the play starts at the ballroom
sweep act1 because act one is one joke told twice
carve cast.brother because the play works without him

# Both endings work. Neither is better. One of them has to go anyway.
draw cast.hero act2.ballroom because only one of them can carry the last scene

# Not an edit. A note, so the next person does not look for a letter that has no sender.
file "the brother's letter" because cutting him left a letter with no sender

floor act3.letter because it is the spine, and everything above was arranged around it
